Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue: "Permission denied" when running a script. Cause: the script is missing the execute bit. Fix with chmod +x /opt/security-scripts/<script_name>.sh and confirm with ls -l that the permissions show x for the owner.

Issue: netstat: command not found. Cause: the net-tools package is not installed. Fix with yum install -y net-tools, or replace netstat -tuln with ss -tuln in the script if the package cannot be installed.

Issue: Cron jobs never seem to execute. Cause: the crond service is stopped, or the crontab was edited but not saved correctly. Verify with systemctl status crond; if inactive, run systemctl enable --now crond. Also confirm entries exist with crontab -l and that each line has exactly five time fields followed by the command.

Issue: firewall-cmd: command not found or firewall commands fail. Cause: firewalld is not installed or not running. Install with yum install -y firewalld and start it with systemctl enable --now firewalld before re-running port_security.sh.

Issue: mail: command not found when testing master_security.sh. Cause: no mail transfer agent is installed. This is non-fatal: send_notification detects the missing binary and logs "Mail not configured - notification skipped" instead of failing. Install mailx only if email notifications are required for your environment.

Issue: security_audit_report.txt is empty or missing sections. Cause: the script was interrupted, or /var/log is not writable by the current user. Confirm you are running as root with whoami, re-run ./security_audit.sh, and check for disk space issues with df -h /var.

Issue: Log files grow very large over time. Cause: no log rotation is configured. Add a logrotate configuration under /etc/logrotate.d/security-scripts that rotates /var/log/*security*.log and /var/log/*patch*.log weekly, or rely on the WARNING messages emitted by cron_monitor.sh when a log exceeds 10MB as a trigger to archive and truncate the file manually.

